# The API is its own Node service, deployed to its own server, so its source,
# tests, scripts and config stay out of the website deployment.
#
# It lives in services/api rather than a top-level api/ directory because
# Vercel builds every file under api/ as a serverless function: the website
# deploy used to try to compile the API's source as individual endpoints.
#
# The exception is the spec behind the API reference (lib/docs/openapi.ts).
# Data and geography pages read the committed docs catalogue projection in
# data/precompiled, so API runtime output stays out of the deployment.
#
# Directory contents are listed rather than the directory itself because an
# ignored directory cannot have a file re-included from it: with
# `/services/api`, the `!` line below is silently ignored and the build fails
# with ENOENT.
/services/api/*
!/services/api/openapi.yaml
